        ":question/id": "23758b8b-9bec-5ac3-b6e8-fa4ac19c5bfc",
        ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $f(x)=12\\ln(2 x)$ at the point $(12,12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$ f=12\\ln u,\\,u=2 x.$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{12}{u},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and we get\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} &=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{u}\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{2 x}\\cdot(2) \\\\ &=\\frac{12}{x}.\\end{aligned}$$\n\nTherefore, the slope $m$ of the tangent line at the point where $x=12$ is\n\n$$m=\\left.(\\frac{12}{x})\\right|_{x=12}=1.$$\n\nHence, the slope of the tangent line at the point $(12,12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)})$ is $m=1.$ Now, we find the equation of the tangent at that point:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}y-y_1 &=m(x-x_1) \\\\ y-(12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}) &=(1)(x-(12)) \\\\ y &=x - 12 + 12 \\log{\\left(24 \\right)}.\\end{aligned}$$"
      },
